# Project Rules for Cursor (Claude / GPT)

You are working on ZeroLeak Tools (`web/003-zeroleak-tools`, zeroleaktools.com).
When working in this repository with Cursor, you MUST strictly adhere to the unified constitution in **[`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md)** as the primary source of truth, followed by the Cursor-specific guidelines below.

---

## 1. Compliance with Universal Constitution (AGENTS.md)
Before planning or executing tasks, carefully review **[`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md)**:
- **Rule 0**: Universal Task Management & Completion Protocol (`HQ_PLAN.md`, `TODO.md` immediate removal, Git history)
- **Rule 1**: Absolute Zero-Network Policy (0-byte server transmission guarantee, CSP `connect-src 'none'`, F12 banner)
- **Rule 2**: Performance & Free Tier Policy (Lighthouse 100, 5-second completion UX, 0 Yen running cost)
- **Rule 3**: 3-Tier Memory Architecture & Legal Defense (`/legal/`)
- **Rule 4**: Above the Fold Usability (3-second start on mobile 375px, header/lead <= 2 lines)
- **Rule 5**: Mobile Scroll Budget (Top page <= 2,000px, slim 64px list items, no duplicate navigation)
- **Rule 6**: 1-Line Tagline Principle (<= 35 chars) & Complete Tool-Below SEO Isolation
- **Rule 7**: ToolShell.astro Governance (Quality budget: 0-byte <= 12, horizontal overflow 0px)
- **Rule 8**: Color Palette Governance (Slate/Emerald base, Blue for ID, Slate for Doc/PDF, Cyan for Dev/Log)
- **Rule 9**: Precision Copywriting (Eliminate vague "safe/secure" buzzwords, write physical/structural facts)
- **Rule 10**: Typography Jump Rate & High Contrast (WCAG AA, no shrinking headings, no light gray body)
- **Rule 11**: Touch Utility (44x44px minimum tap target) & SGO/GEO By Design (`llms.txt`, JSON-LD)
- **Rule 12**: 10 Production Tools Registry & New Tool Integration Checklist

---

## 2. Cursor Specific Execution Rules

### ① Build & Automated Verification
Always verify the operational integrity and quality budget before finishing tasks:
```bash
npm run build
node --experimental-strip-types scripts/verify_operations.mjs
```

### ② Task & Git Commit Protocol
- Remove finished items from `TODO.md` immediately upon fulfilling completion criteria.
- Use Conventional Commits (`feat(...)`, `fix(...)`, `refactor(...)`, `chore(...)`).
- Always push changes to remote (`git push origin main`) to trigger Cloudflare Pages deployment.

### ③ Single Source of Truth
- Never duplicate universal rules across `GEMINI.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, and `.cursorrules`. Always update **`AGENTS.md`** as the sole constitutional document.
